#: ../../repository.rst:86
msgid "Translate with Guidedog"
msgstr "Traducir con Guidedog"

#: ../../repository.rst:99
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Translate and review `msgstr` values in the PO files. Guidedog "
#| "extracts POT files, merges catalogs, reports progress, and builds each "
#| "edition. It does not invent translations. Commands, paths, code, API "
#| "names, and reference targets stay unchanged. Only the manual and "
#| "repository overview are translated; API and GDS remain English. See "
#| "the [manual build instructions](howto/maintain-docs.rst) for "
#| "assembling all editions and PDF books."
msgid ""
"Translate and review ``msgstr`` values in the PO files. Guidedog extracts "
"POT files, merges catalogs, reports progress, and builds each edition. It "
"does not invent translations. Commands, paths, code, API names, and "
"reference targets stay unchanged. Only the manual and repository overview "
"are translated. API and GDS remain English. See the :doc:`manual build "
"instructions <howto/maintain-docs>` for assembling all editions and PDF "
"books."
msgstr ""
"Traduzca y revise los valores `msgstr` de los archivos PO. Guidedog "
"extrae POT, fusiona catálogos, informa del progreso y compila cada "
"edición; no redacta traducciones. Mantenga comandos, rutas, código, "
"nombres de API y destinos de referencia. Solo se traducen el manual y el "
"resumen del repositorio; API y GDS siguen en inglés. Véanse las "
"[instrucciones de compilación](howto/maintain-docs.rst) para reunir las "
"ediciones y los PDF."

#: ../../repository.rst:105
msgid "Extend and publish"
msgstr ""

#: ../../repository.rst:108
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Write your own publisher with the {doc}`step-by-step plugin chapter "
#| "<plugins>`. Start with a working folder publisher, then follow the "
#| "real GitHub Pages implementation through ownership, credentials, "
#| "conditional updates and recovery. `guidedog publish --timeout=SECONDS` "
#| "bounds each complete exchange (default: 300 seconds); choose a value "
#| "longer than `--wait`. After an unknown outcome, recover before "
#| "publishing again."
msgid ""
"Write a build plugin or a publisher with the :doc:`step-by-step plugin "
"chapter <plugins>`. A plugin implements one Rust trait. The same value is "
"linked into a custom ``guidedog`` binary with ``gd_cli::run_with``, or "
"served as an installed program with ``gd_plugins::serve_plugin``. The "
"chapter then follows the real GitHub Pages publisher through ownership, "
"credentials, conditional updates and recovery. ``guidedog publish "
"--timeout=SECONDS`` bounds each complete exchange (default: 300 seconds). "
"We choose a value longer than ``--wait``. After an unknown outcome, we "
"recover before publishing again."
msgstr ""
"Para escribir tu propio publicador, sigue el {doc}`capítulo paso a paso "
"sobre plugins <plugins>`. Empieza con un publicador de carpetas que "
"funciona y después recorre la implementación real de GitHub Pages: "
"propiedad de los recursos, credenciales, actualizaciones condicionales y "
"recuperación. `guidedog publish --timeout=SECONDS` limita cada "
"intercambio completo; el valor predeterminado es 300 segundos y debe "
"superar `--wait`. Si el resultado es desconocido, ejecuta la recuperación "
"antes de volver a publicar."

#: ../../repository.rst:117
msgid "Keep discussions"
msgstr "Mantener discusiones"

#: ../../repository.rst:120
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "`dsc` keeps proposals and decisions as reStructuredText records, one "
#| "file each, and builds them into a website and PDF books with Guidedog. "
#| "Each catalog has a prefix: Guidedog's design records use `gds`, and "
#| "another project might use `eds`."
msgid ""
"``dsc`` keeps proposals and decisions as reStructuredText records, one "
"file each. It builds them into a website and PDF books with Guidedog. "
"Each catalog has a prefix: Guidedog's design records use ``gds``, and "
"another project might use ``eds``."
msgstr ""
"`dsc` guarda propuestas y decisiones como registros reStructuredText, un "
"archivo por registro, y los convierte con Guidedog en un sitio web y "
"libros PDF. Cada catálogo tiene un prefijo: los registros de diseño de "
"Guidedog usan `gds`, y otro proyecto podría usar `eds`."

#: ../../repository.rst:133
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "A catalog's `discussion.toml` sets its lifecycle states, record types, "
#| "and numbering, and `dsc config` prints it. `dsc` comes in the Guidedog "
#| "archive and builds with the installed `guidedog`. `dscc` is `dsc` with "
#| "Guidedog built in, for a machine with nothing else installed; each "
#| "release has a `dscc` archive for every platform. `guidedog gds` runs "
#| "the same commands on Guidedog's own `docs/gds`. See [Keep a discussion "
#| "catalog](howto/discussions.rst)."
msgid ""
"A catalog's ``discussion.toml`` sets its lifecycle states, record types, "
"and numbering. ``dsc config`` prints it. ``dsc`` comes in the Guidedog "
"archive and builds with the installed ``guidedog``. ``dscc`` is ``dsc`` "
"with Guidedog built in, for a machine with nothing else installed. "
"``guidedog gds`` runs the same commands on Guidedog's own ``docs/gds``. "
"See :doc:`Keep a discussion catalog <howto/discussions>`."
msgstr ""
"El `discussion.toml` de un catálogo fija los estados de su ciclo de vida, "
"sus tipos de registro y su numeración, y `dsc config` lo muestra. `dsc` "
"viene en el archivo de Guidedog y compila con el `guidedog` instalado. "
"`dscc` es `dsc` con Guidedog integrado, para una máquina sin nada más "
"instalado; cada versión incluye un archivo `dscc` para cada plataforma. "
"`guidedog gds` ejecuta los mismos comandos sobre `docs/gds`, el catálogo "
"propio de Guidedog. Consulte [Mantener un catálogo de "
"discusiones](howto/discussions.rst)."

